{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NjM2MjI=","is_bot":false,"login":"mfateev","name":"Maxim Fateev"},"body":"docker-compose up and other ways to start a service should produce a clear message into the log that indicates that service is up and running. Something like:\r\n```\r\n _____                                    _  \r\n|_   _|__ _ __ ___  _ __   ___  _ __ __ _| | \r\n  | |/ _ \\ '_ ` _ \\| '_ \\ / _ \\| '__/ _` | | \r\n  | |  __/ | | | | | |_) | (_) | | | (_| | | \r\n  |_|\\___|_| |_| |_| .__/ \\___/|_|  \\__,_|_| \r\n                   |_|                       \r\n ____  _             _           _ \r\n/ ___|| |_ __ _ _ __| |_ ___  __| |\r\n\\___ \\| __/ _` | '__| __/ _ \\/ _` |\r\n ___) | || (_| | |  | ||  __/ (_| |\r\n|____/ \\__\\__,_|_|   \\__\\___|\\__,_|\r\n```","closedAt":"2026-01-25T16:44:32Z","comments":[{"id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYwNDA4OTMyMw==","author":{"login":"shawnhathaway"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Docker Configuration link: https://docs.docker.com/config/containers/logging/configure/","createdAt":"2020-03-25T21:10:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/temporalio/temporal/issues/19#issuecomment-604089323","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDODNqesM7iUIaR","author":{"login":"yiminc"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"The recommended way for local development is now the [Temporal CLI](https://docs.temporal.io/cli), which provides the clear startup feedback described here:\n\n```\n$ temporal server start-dev\nCLI 1.5.1 (Server 1.29.1, UI 2.42.1)\n\nServer:  localhost:7233\nUI:      http://localhost:8233\nMetrics: http://localhost:62195/metrics\n```\n\nThis single-binary experience clearly indicates when the server is ready and shows the endpoints for the server, UI, and metrics.\n\nFor production deployments, server readiness can be verified through health check endpoints.\n\nGiven that the CLI now addresses the local development use case, we're going to close this issue. If there are specific scenarios where additional startup messaging would be helpful that aren't covered by the CLI, please feel free to open a new issue with those details.","createdAt":"2026-01-25T16:44:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/temporalio/temporal/issues/19#issuecomment-3796928145","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2019-11-15T01:05:59Z","labels":[{"id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjIxMDMwNzg3","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"},{"id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDE5OTE0ODQ5","name":"docker","description":"","color":"eda6d4"},{"id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDE5OTIzNjU1","name":"devexp","description":"","color":"9350b7"},{"id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNTc2NTM1ODQ2","name":"difficulty: easy","description":"","color":"68d662"},{"id":"LA_kwDODNqesM8AAAABGnRdBw","name":"P2","description":"","color":"FBCA04"}],"milestone":null,"number":19,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"CLOSED","title":"Clear indication that service is up and running","updatedAt":"2026-01-25T16:44:32Z","url":"https://github.com/temporalio/temporal/issues/19"}
